    rationale:
      "Dispatched a research agent (general-purpose, read-only) briefed on AGENT_PROTOCOL's full priority order (fold sibling > sold-capability wiring gap > Convex/SQLite parity > security/injection audit > untested orchestration > docs clarity) and told which recent angles had already gone clean, and asked it to find one concrete, previously-unaddressed gap small enough for a single focused iteration. It found a real tier-1 sold-capability wiring gap: src/lib/commerce/catalog.ts's normalizeCommerceItems captures and length-caps (MAX_SKU_DESCRIPTION_LENGTH=280) an operator-entered SKU description, and src/components/preview/commerce-catalog.tsx renders it on the public storefront card — but src/lib/commerce/stripe-sync.ts's syncCommerceCatalogToStripe never forwarded it anywhere near Stripe: products.create only ever sent name+metadata, and the existing commerce-sku-stripe-product-name-resync fix (PR #817) extended the resync diff to cover a changed businessName/SKU name but never touched description either. src/app/api/commerce/checkout/route.ts creates the Buy now Checkout Session from `price: item.stripePriceId` alone — Stripe's own hosted Checkout page renders the Product's description, so a shopper saw the operator's helpful detail on the storefront card and then had it silently vanish the moment they clicked through to the actual payment page where money changes hands. A small, real conversion/trust gap on a live revenue path, not a hypothetical one, and directly analogous to the already-fixed name-resync bug (same function, same missing-field pattern) rather than requiring any new invented facts or policy. Verified the finding directly before implementing: read stripe-sync.ts, catalog.ts, commerce-catalog.tsx, and the commerce checkout route myself and confirmed the missing field end to end. Shipped: added `description?: string | null` to MinimalStripeProduct and `description?: string` to the products.create/update param types in stripe-sync.ts; products.create now includes description when the SKU has a non-empty trimmed one; the existing `product.name !== desiredName` resync check was widened to `product.name !== desiredName || (product.description ?? undefined) !== desiredDescription`, and the update call now always sends both name and description (description defaulting to `\"\"` to clear a removed one) — mirroring the exact no-op-comparison-not-unconditional-call pattern the name resync already established, so an unchanged re-sync still makes zero extra Stripe API calls. Extended the fake Stripe test double in stripe-sync.test.ts to track/return description on create and update, and added 3 new cases: description included on create when present, omitted when absent, and resynced in place on a later change (asserting the Product/Price ids stay stable, mirroring the existing name-resync test's shape) — renamed the adjacent 'does not call products.update when unchanged' test to cover both fields. Added one paragraph to /docs/architecture's existing commerce-sku-stripe-product-name-resync writeup documenting the same fix for description, right where a reader would already be looking. Verified: npm ci (409 packages, 9 known high-severity findings, unchanged dev-only) + npx tsc --noEmit (0 errors) + npm run lint (clean) + npx vitest run full suite (3339 passed, up from 3336, 209 files unchanged — 3 new cases in stripe-sync.test.ts) + a full production build (npm run build, clean, same 43-route ○/ƒ split, no new warnings). No dev-server smoke test needed beyond the existing Vitest coverage: this is server-only orchestration logic behind a fake Stripe client, with no new UI/route surface to click through (the storefront description display and the checkout-page rendering both already worked and are unchanged by this fix — only what gets sent TO Stripe changed). NEXT_STEPS unchanged — all five gated items (stripe-price-objects, lead-ingestion, marketing-content-scheduling, commerce-payouts-stripe-connect, github-actions-runner-unavailable) remain operator/legal/infra-blocked; this closes a sold-capability wiring gap, not any of the five gated items. Diff-gate anchor moves to 1490c23c (this session's own starting tip, post-PR-#826).",
